      "text": [
        "4902 - وَ قَالَ رَسُولُ اَللَّهِ صَلَّى اَللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ آلِهِ :\n\"مَنْ أَرَادَ اَلْبَقَاءَ وَ لاَ بَقَاءَ فَلْيُبَاكِرِ اَلْغَدَاءَ وَ لْيُجَوِّدِ اَلْحِذَاءَ وَ لْيُخَفِّفِ اَلرِّدَاءَ وَ لْيُقِلَّ مُجَامَعَةَ اَلنِّسَاءِ، \" قِيلَ يَا رَسُولَ اَللَّهِ وَ مَا خِفَّةُ اَلرِّدَاءِ قَالَ \"قِلَّةُ اَلدَّيْنِ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4902 - The Messenger of Allah (swt) (peace be upon him and his family) said:\n\"Whoever desires longevity, though there is no permanence, should have an early breakfast, wear well-made shoes, wear a light cloak, and reduce intimacy with women.\"\nIt was asked: \"O Messenger of Allah (swt), what is meant by wearing a light cloak?\"\nImam (as) replied: \"It means having little debt.\""
        ]
      }
    },
